## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook example of **"coverage theater"** — every production method is called (achieving line coverage) but almost nothing is *verified*. Here's the severity-ranked list:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — No Behavioral Assertions

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Bug It Misses |
|---|------|-------------|---------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **Fire-and-forget** — no assert at all | `Save()` could silently no-op; duplicates never caught |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33-35) | **Fire-and-forget** — calls method, never checks result | Price could remain unchanged; wrong product updated |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38-41) | **Fire-and-forget** | Product could still exist after removal |
| 4 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | **Fire-and-forget** | Discount could apply wrong math (e.g., `Price * fraction` instead of `Price * (1 - fraction)`) |
| 5 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | **Fire-and-forget** | Parsing could corrupt data; fields could be swapped |
| 6 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | **No assert, not even `IsNotNull`** | Could return -1 or throw and this test still "passes" (it assigns to a discarded local) |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")?.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnfindable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Weak/Meaningless Assertions

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Why It's Dangerous |
|---|------|-------------|--------------------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L26-29) | **Assert-on-type-not-value** — only checks `IsNotNull` | Would pass even if the wrong product is returned |
