### Summary

The root cause is a single systemic anti-pattern: **"exercise-only" tests** that call production code to hit coverage lines without asserting outcomes. This gives false confidence — 95% coverage, 0% confidence. Every test here needs the three-part **Arrange → Act → Assert** structure, with assertions on *values* not just *non-nullity*.
